        Root cause:
        The root cause of the bug was the introduction of unnecessary memory barriers in the `_local()` variants of the `xchg` and `cmpxchg` operations on the Alpha architecture. These barriers were added in previous commits, which disrupted the intended memory ordering and could lead to incorrect behavior in concurrent operations. The original implementation avoided these barriers to ensure efficient execution, and their presence caused memory ordering bugs.

        Commit message:
        locking/xchg/alpha: Remove superfluous memory barriers from
 the _local() variants

The following two commits:

  79d442461df74 ("locking/xchg/alpha: Clean up barrier usage by using smp_mb() in place of __ASM__MB")
  472e8c55cf662 ("locking/xchg/alpha: Fix xchg() and cmpxchg() memory ordering bugs")

... ended up adding unnecessary barriers to the _local() variants on Alpha,
which the previous code took care to avoid.

Fix them by adding the smp_mb() into the cmpxchg() macro rather than into the
____cmpxchg() variants.

